The repository is organized into shared model definitions, policy generation modules, evaluation routines, visualization tools, and run scripts. 
Specifically, \texttt{data/} stores reservoir characteristics, rating curves, inflow datasets, and penalty settings; 
\texttt{src/reservoir\_benchmark/shared/} contains the common reservoir model; 
\texttt{src/reservoir\_benchmark/policy\_generation/} implements four scheduling methods under \texttt{dp/}, \texttt{sdp/}, \texttt{iso\_surf/}, and \texttt{dqn/}; 
\texttt{src/reservoir\_benchmark/evaluation/} provides the corresponding evaluation runners; 
\texttt{outputs/policy\_generation/} and \texttt{outputs/evaluation/} store trained artifacts and assessment results; 
and \texttt{src/reservoir\_benchmark/visualization/} together with \texttt{scripts/run\_visualization.py} generates manuscript figures.

Input files are provided in \texttt{.csv}, \texttt{.xlsx}, \texttt{.txt}, and \texttt{.yaml} formats. 
Output files include result tables in \texttt{.csv}/\texttt{.xlsx}, trained DQN model checkpoints (e.g., \texttt{.pth}), preprocessed data, and publication figures in PDF format. 
Example input datasets required to run the benchmark (excluding inflow series) are included in the repository.

The main figures and tables reported in this paper can be reproduced using the visualization scripts under \texttt{src/reservoir\_benchmark/visualization/} (launched via \texttt{scripts/run\_visualization.py}) and the instructions documented in the repository README. 
The mapping between manuscript figures/tables and scripts is explicitly documented in \texttt{README.md}. 
The scripts \texttt{scripts/run\_policy\_generation.py} and \texttt{scripts/run\_evaluation.py} reproduce the method sweeps and the standardized evaluation workflow.
